  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In a turbulent-flow bubble inheritance, Fang Yuan saves a single surviving rank six Immortal Gu from a dark green lump held by a bone-path skeleton. Fragmented thoughts name it Perceivable Dao. It is an information path investigative Immortal Gu with a niche effect: it lets the user see what types of dao marks a target has and how many.",
        "chapters": [
          1156
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "On first use, starlight gathers into shining water over Fang Yuan’s body for more than ten breaths, then fades, and he receives counts of the dao marks in his body. Used on Immortal Gu, the starry water covers them but returns no result, because Immortal Gu hold Great Dao fragments rather than ordinary dao marks. On mortal Gu it works. On immortal materials it can sense dao marks, with higher immortal essence cost when the material is higher quality or not information path. Fang Yuan judges it cannot be used on Immortal Gu, costs more against conflicting dao marks in materials, and is slow and conspicuous when probing another Gu Immortal.",
        "chapters": [
          1161
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "first-test",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      }
    ]
